      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OLE MISS (4) resumes after making good progress last time in. Blinkers come off and can finish over the top of these with the two trials under her belt. Go close. FIRE 'N' STONE (3) big jump in grade third up when she dropped out quickly to run last over 1350m at Beaumont (Newcastle). Pulled up with cardiac arrhythmia on that occasion and finds a much weaker contest. Likely to play a big role. JAZZ ALL KNIGHT (1) tough mare who comes back a few grades today from the good gate. Just under a month between runs when she tired late to finish fifth over 1200m at Goulburn in BM66 class.  Can take control here and prove hard to run down. HONEY SLIDER (2) deep into the prep and racing in career-best form. Snagged back early and launched late to get the job done over 1300m at Narromine. Will be tough to stop again with the claim. BROGANS CREEK (9) is struggling for form and assess on the handy fifth three starts back.",
